# Next.js

- App Router only. Route groups: `(store)`, `(account)`, `(checkout)`, `(corporate)`, `admin`, `api`.
- Default to Server Components. Client components are for drawers, quantity, and interactive forms only.
- Mutations: Server Actions or route handlers. Do not fetch catalogues in `useEffect`.
- Business logic lives in `src/features/*` and `src/lib/*`. UI does not call Paystack or recompute legal totals.
- Admin routes: server-side role check before render. Hidden nav is not security.
- Prefer `generateMetadata` and JSON-LD on product/category/brand pages. See @docs/SEO.md.
- Route handlers for external callers only (`/api/paystack/webhook`, uploads). No public GraphQL or generic REST storefront API.
